#A team of autonomous robots collaborates to accomplish a complex task (e.g., search and
rescue, package delivery) in a dynamic and uncertain environment. Implement multiagent
reinforcement learning algorithms (e.g., MADDPG, COMA) to enable the robots to
coordinate their actions and achieve collective objectives efficiently. Write a Python
program to simulate the robots&#39; interactions and evaluate their performance in completing
the task.


import numpy as np

np.random.seed(1)

robots = 3
targets = np.array([[8, 8], [2, 8], [8, 2]])
positions = np.random.randint(0, 10, (robots, 2))

print("Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning")
print("Algorithm: MADDPG-style Coordination\n")

for episode in range(50):

    for i in range(robots):

        # Move toward assigned target
        if positions[i, 0] < targets[i, 0]:
            positions[i, 0] += 1
        elif positions[i, 0] > targets[i, 0]:
            positions[i, 0] -= 1

        if positions[i, 1] < targets[i, 1]:
            positions[i, 1] += 1
        elif positions[i, 1] > targets[i, 1]:
            positions[i, 1] -= 1

# Evaluate performance
distance = np.sum(
    np.linalg.norm(positions - targets, axis=1)
)

completed = np.sum(
    np.all(positions == targets, axis=1)
)

print("Final Robot Positions:")
print(positions)

print("\nTargets:")
print(targets)

print("\nRobots Completed:", completed, "/", robots)
print("Total Distance:", round(distance, 2))

if completed == robots:
    print("Collective Task: SUCCESS")
else:
    print("Collective Task: PARTIALLY COMPLETED")
